  "result": "I've found the cause of the odd option order but haven't changed any code, since plan mode is on. The plan is written to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-serialized-dongarra.md`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts option names with `reverse=True`. That puts the long form first, so `--help` shows `--verbose, -v` instead of `-v, --verbose`.\n\n**Fix:** Change `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)` to `rv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])`. The sort is stable, so names with the same prefix length keep the order they were declared in.\n\n**Not run yet:** I haven't run `pytest`, and I haven't checked `--help` output on a sample command. The plan lists both as the check after the fix.\n\nI couldn't call ExitPlanMode in this session. Please approve the plan so I can make the one-line edit and run the tests.",
